WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
- Your daughter just
went to college, right?

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.753
- Yes.

00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:03.750
- [Kelly] Are you stressed about that?

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.460
My daughter's seven and
I'm already freaking out.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.110
- Stressed is not even the word.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:07.943
- [Kelly] 'Cause their on their own.

00:00:07.943 --> 00:00:09.690
- It's the only time I've
ever regretted children.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.523
Having them.

00:00:10.523 --> 00:00:12.450
- I have sons, so I feel
like it'll be less stressful.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.522
- [Kelly] Oh, no, you're
gonna get so many calls.

00:00:14.522 --> 00:00:15.355
- [Brooke] You think that-

00:00:15.355 --> 00:00:17.803
- Oh, God. I feel like all I
have to worry about is like,

00:00:17.803 --> 00:00:18.636
don't hit your head right now.

00:00:18.636 --> 00:00:20.040
- [Kelly] 'Cause you send
them out there and you hope

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.070
you've done your best and I'm
just freaking out about it.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.300
And it's so far away.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.505
- The driving away from them-

00:00:27.505 --> 00:00:28.350
- [Kelly] (whispers
quietly) You're leaving.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.760
- In college, it was like
I had been just gut punched

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.460
and I couldn't, well, I was just,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.780
I choke sobbed, that like,
ugly crying in the car.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.650
My husband was so funny, he
said, okay so, when we go home,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.900
would you rather cry in the car

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.450
or would you rather cry in a plane?

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.220
And I was like, I need a car.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.830
I can't be on a public
plane and be with people.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:53.663
- [Kelly] Sobbing.

00:00:53.663 --> 00:00:55.350
- Sobbing. They'll think
something's wrong with me.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.628
So, yeah, and then you see them thriving,

00:00:58.628 --> 00:01:01.581
and they don't have time for you anymore.

00:01:01.581 --> 00:01:03.320
And you're just like,

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.934
(faux crying) I'm so
happy you're so happy.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.622
- [Kelly] (faux crying) I'm so
happy you're so independent.

00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:09.300
- [Brooke] (faux crying) How dare you.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.640
I mean, I was never that independent.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.920
You know, I mean, I was
sick, missing my mom.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.440
And so the fact that she,
in a way I have envy -

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.110
- [Kelly] I have karma coming
my way, I was so independent.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.880
My kids are both gonna never call me.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.990
- [Brooke] No.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.610
- [Kelly] I was so
independent and I love that.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.250
You love that you raised
independent little beings-

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.083
- [Kirsten] Healthier, really.

00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:29.310
- But at the same time,
you're like, need me a little.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.100
- And they do. Then you'll
get the crying phone call.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.340
Or the, you know, and then
you're sort of like, oh well,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.630
okay, they still need me.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.863
But you don't want them
unhappy, but she's thriving.

00:01:39.863 --> 00:01:41.190
- [Kelly] That's exciting.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.990
- Yeah, and it's just, it's one of those-

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.760
- Like her whole world is before her.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:45.593
That's exciting as a mom, yeah.

00:01:45.593 --> 00:01:47.280
- Yeah, and she's doing
all these activities,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.590
and she's playing intermural sports,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.450
and she's trying out for the musical.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.670
So it's really, it's, but I will say

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:57.480
I never thought it would
be that hard to just-

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.920
- [Kelly] I know it's gonna be hard.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.680
- It's so hard to be in
the house without them.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.320
- I just said my daughter
seven, she's nowhere near this

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.450
and I'm already freaking out about it.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.220
because it's just so weird
when you have them around

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.930
and it's your every day and then-

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:14.069
- And now I'm just with the
15 year old, which is a joy.

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:14.908
- [Kirsten] Oh gosh.

00:02:14.908 --> 00:02:16.620
(everyone laughs)

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.453
- [Kelly] Every second.

00:02:17.453 --> 00:02:20.880
- 15 is such an easy age for
girls, and their mothers.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.020
- [Kirsten] Especially in Los Angeles.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.215
- [Brooke] Oh we get along and-

00:02:24.215 --> 00:02:25.173
- Instagram and all that.

00:02:25.173 --> 00:02:26.006
- [Kelly] Oh my God,

00:02:26.006 --> 00:02:27.690
there's so much to look forward to for me.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:29.460
So wait, so let's talk about the positive.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.626
Your new movie, your new
Netflix movie, is called

00:02:32.626 --> 00:02:34.380
- [Kelly And Brooke] A
Castle for Christmas.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.610
- [Kelly] A Castle for Christmas,

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.170
which is what I want for Christmas.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.870
- It's a good thing to
want and they're for sale

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:40.703
all over the place.

00:02:40.703 --> 00:02:43.753
- [Kelly] They are, you
a Zillow porn person?

00:02:43.753 --> 00:02:44.724
- Love it.

00:02:44.724 --> 00:02:46.710
- [Kelly] We probably
can't say that on here,

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.540
but I literally, I'm in love with Zillow.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.190
I call it Zillow porn.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.320
There are castles and chateaus,
it's the craziest thing,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.460
they'll probably edit this out,

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.260
but you can look them
up and they're for sale.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.500
- I know, and what's interesting,
so we were in Scotland

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.760
smack in the middle of COVID.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.400
And we were in a bubble.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.680
So we were just with these people

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.540
and we all lived sort of in the same place

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.660
but they had me in a house, a first house.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.320
And then, I ended up moving
to the carriage house

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.380
of a neighboring castle,
which was amazing.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.260
But the first house, I
was alone in this house

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.091
and I'd go to bed at
night and I'd hear like

00:03:22.091 --> 00:03:23.940
(scratching noises)

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.080
And I was like, what's that sound?

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.213
It must be birds on the
roof or something like that.

00:03:27.213 --> 00:03:28.830
- Like a Snow White moment.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:29.976
- Or something, yeah, something.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:30.809
Turns out I called the -

00:03:30.809 --> 00:03:32.230
- Little mice, making you a dress.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.832
- Yeah, yeah, basically.

00:03:33.832 --> 00:03:36.120
(laughing) Making me my dress.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.770
And I called man who owned the place,

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:41.100
and I was like, hey, you
know, what's on the roof?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.140
And he's like, oh yeah, the
house is haunted (laughing).

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:43.996
I was like, I'm sorry, what?

00:03:43.996 --> 00:03:44.829
- [Kelly] Wait, what?

00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:47.880
- And he said, yeah, well,
but don't worry, it's a dog.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.040
And I was like, oh, that
makes it so much better

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.660
to have it be a dog.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.450
And I was like, okay, well
I'm glad it's a friendly dog

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.880
but I'm not gonna stay here anymore.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.963
I had to move because I
started getting all my mind-

00:03:58.963 --> 00:04:01.410
- I love how he tried to make that normal.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.360
- I know. And then when I
looked around the house,

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.140
I realized that all the
pictures were little, this dog.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.570
And there was like dog
mugs and dog magnets

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.130
and this little Scotty dog.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.590
And I was like, yeah, you know what?

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:14.730
I don't wanna do this.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.710
- Do they keep the pictures
around to not anger it?

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.720
- [Brooke] I guess. It was a happy dog.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.090
I mean there, it wasn't
like menacing or anything,

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:21.930
but definitely.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:25.470
So then I moved to the carriage
house of an actual castle.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:26.557
Which was, oh, I pretended-

00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:28.800
- Even more haunted. No, I'm sure-

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.000
- It sounds so romantic,
like the best movie ever.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.740
- I pretended I was an Outlander.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.088
- Ah, yeah, exactly.

00:04:33.088 --> 00:04:36.060
- I was drinking whiskey and
wrapping myself in blankets.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:36.893
- [Kelly] Oh, I love that.

00:04:36.893 --> 00:04:41.100
- And every Friday, the guys
would, those transpo guys,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.550
would come to the set in kilts.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.660
- Oh my gosh, that's attractive.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.666
- And they're these
unbelievably tough, great guys.

00:04:49.666 --> 00:04:50.520
- [Kelly] Oh, okay.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.060
- And they were in these skirts
and you're like, this works.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.530
- [Kelly] You really are on Outlander.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.300
- [Brooke] You really, oh yeah.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.250
I'm like, is it true, under?

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.982
- Is it true? Is it just, yep.

00:05:00.982 --> 00:05:02.378
- Is it true, Brooke?

00:05:02.378 --> 00:05:05.010
- Some of them it was,
yeah, not all of them.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.113
I guess it's up to your discretion.

